WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
- Welcome back, y'all,

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.023
to the end of my surprise
40th birthday show.

00:00:04.023 --> 00:00:05.013
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:06.578
I'm sad it's ending,

00:00:06.578 --> 00:00:07.980
but it was a really great time.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.100
I love it so much,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.410
it's gonna take me at
least an hour to finish off

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.440
the rest of that queso fountain alone,

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.030
in my dressing room, please.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.174
Okay, maybe 45 minutes.
(audience laughs)

00:00:17.174 --> 00:00:18.280
Which reminds me,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.370
it's time for "What I'm Liking".

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.080
(upbeat music)
(audience applauds)

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.597
All right, so we've got Tampa-based,

00:00:24.597 --> 00:00:27.870
MOR TV on-air personality
Jason Guy on the line,

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.210
who's gonna guide me along.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.449
So Jason, great to meet you.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:33.060
- Hi!
(audience cheers)

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.106
- [Kelly] So where are you?

00:00:34.106 --> 00:00:35.190
- It's great to meet you, Kelly.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.320
Sending you happy birthday wishes from

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:41.340
the eighth-annual Pier
60 Sugar Sand Festival.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.420
You might be jealous here,

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.568
I'm in sunny Clearwater Beach, Florida.

00:00:45.568 --> 00:00:46.401
- Yes, I am.

00:00:46.401 --> 00:00:47.700
- This is a huge festival,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.117
it brings in 200,000 people over 17 days.

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:54.810
People enjoy walking on that pier.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.020
Just think about that stroll.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.780
You can ride a Ferris wheel here,

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:58.840
or even relax on the beach.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.280
But the real star is sugar sand,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.450
Clearwater's most famous natural asset.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.490
And, Kelly, you gotta see this!

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.589
It looks and feels just like real sugar.

00:01:11.589 --> 00:01:13.621
Ah, it's amazing here.

00:01:13.621 --> 00:01:16.505
And sand sculptors come
from all around the world

00:01:16.505 --> 00:01:20.240
to create amazing works
of art out of sand.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.180
So this year we're taking
the sand and animals

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.310
and creating a theme of Sandimals.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.143
- You like that?
- What?

00:01:26.143 --> 00:01:27.460
- So I'm here in this tent,

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.410
its 21,000 square feet of sculptures.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.663
There are 150 of them in here.

00:01:33.663 --> 00:01:37.620
Everything from an aardvark
to a zebra in here.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.110
And I've got some cool dolphins behind me.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:41.570
Look at this giant dolphin-
- Amazing!

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.180
- And some other marine animals.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:47.337
And it all pays tribute to the
Clearwater Marine Aquarium.

00:01:47.337 --> 00:01:49.360
- I love it, oh, I love an aquarium!

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.453
I'm a huge fan.
(audience applauds)

00:01:50.453 --> 00:01:52.720
So tell me about that aquarium.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.140
- Okay, so the Clearwater Marine Aquarium

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.050
is a great place

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.680
that not only takes in these
sick and injured animals,

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.140
but they work to rehabilitate them

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.660
and hopefully release them,

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.550
so it's really great the
aquarium gets this tribute.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.713
It's a great way to honor

00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:09.936
all of the good and amazing
work that they're doing here.

00:02:09.936 --> 00:02:14.533
Now, there is one thing that's
happening at this festival,

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:18.300
there is a Sandimal sculpture
that hasn't been revealed

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.802
to the public, yet.

00:02:19.802 --> 00:02:24.410
It is a "Kelly Clarkson Show" exclusive.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.898
- Oh my god! (laughs)
- Are you ready for this?

00:02:25.898 --> 00:02:27.710
For your birthday,

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.734
Happy Birthday!
- Oh my god!

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:30.567
(Kelly laughs)
(audience cheers)

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.777
We've got Henry as a Sandimal.
(audience cheers)

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:34.708
- Oh, you have Henry!

00:02:34.708 --> 00:02:36.431
- [Jason] And of course,
Henry's best friend.

00:02:36.431 --> 00:02:38.264
- You included my dog!

00:02:38.264 --> 00:02:40.270
That's so nice.

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:41.560
Oh my gosh, I love that.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.990
- I know, this guy and all of Florida say

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.290
Happy Birthday Kelly.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.610
- Well thank you so much.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.220
Oh my gosh, it was so nice.
(audience cheers)

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.527
Thank you to Jason Guy,
Tampa-based MOR TV,

00:02:51.527 --> 00:02:54.007
and the Pier 60 Sugar Sand
Festival in Clearwater Beach,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:55.420
I wish I was there right now.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.000
I'm liking that post right now.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:57.833
(love react button dings)

00:02:57.833 --> 00:02:58.666
And that's not all,

00:02:58.666 --> 00:03:00.980
our season-long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.890
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.702
wanna celebrate those creating fearlessly,

00:03:04.702 --> 00:03:08.070
which is exactly what the
Pier 60 Sugar Sand Festival

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:08.903
is all about,

00:03:08.903 --> 00:03:10.210
so they're writing a check to the

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.184
Sunsets at Pier 60 Society for $1000.

00:03:12.184 --> 00:03:13.017
(audience applauds)

00:03:13.017 --> 00:03:16.007
So love you, thank you for that, Pilot.

